==============================================================================
PART 3.  The empirical test at p = 24..36 (the convergent desert)
==============================================================================
  Recipe of 12.8.6.2 + 12.8.6.3, reimplemented independently; candidate
  n taken from the whole window (ordinary integers) rather than from
  the continued-fraction chain. Correction search in log space; every
  reported pass is re-verified with exact big integers, all p rotations,
  plus the exact divisibility test q | R_r.

  Assembled from the slices listed in staircase_allp_diophantine_note.txt.
  Rows p = 18..22 are cross-checks against 12.8.6.4's own range, not part of
  the brief's requested sweep. The 'cap' column says whether the sharpening
  pass hit its wall-clock budget: 'yes' means the gamma in that row is the
  sharpest found INSIDE the budget, an upper bound on the sharpest achievable
  gamma, not a measurement of it.

